   "source": [
    "# === Paso 5: graficar una lista con los batch a observar ===\n",
    "measurement_list_dic = list_measurements(hdf5_path)\n",
    "\n",
    "measurement_list_names = [measurement[\"name\"] for measurement in measurement_list_dic if measurement[\"mode\"] == \"transfer\"]\n",
    "print(measurement_list_names)\n",
    "\n",
    "measurements_name_issue = []\n",
    "\n",
    "for measurement_name in measurement_list_names:\n",
    "    try:\n",
    "        plot_transfer(hdf5_path, measurement_name)\n",
    "    except TypeError:\n",
    "        print(f\"Couldn't plot {measurement_name} due to a TypeError\")\n",
    "        measurements_name_issue.append(measurement_name)\n",
    "        continue"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "## Extracci\u00f3n de par\u00e1metros\n",
    "\n",
    "### $V_{th}$ \u2014 $\\sqrt{I_{DS}}$ (saturaci\u00f3n)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Marco te\u00f3rico: Reg\u00edmenes de operaci\u00f3n del FET\n",
    "\n",
    "En un transistor de efecto de campo, la operaci\u00f3n se divide en dos reg\u00edmenes seg\u00fan la condici\u00f3n:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|V_{DS}| \\geq |V_{GS} - V_{th}| \\quad \\text{(saturaci\u00f3n)}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "En **saturaci\u00f3n**, y suponiendo movilidad constante, la corriente drenaje-fuente sigue la **ley cuadr\u00e1tica**:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$|I_{DS}^{sat}| = \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\mu_{sat}\\,C\\,\\frac{W}{L}\\,(V_{GS} - V_{th})^2$$\n",
    "\n",
    "Donde:\n",
    "- $\\mu_{sat}$: movilidad de los portadores en saturaci\u00f3n (cm\u00b2/V\u00b7s)\n",
    "- $C$: capacitancia por unidad de \u00e1rea de la doble capa el\u00e9ctrica (F/cm\u00b2). En un EGOFET es mucho mayor que en un MOSFET porque la EDL es del orden de nan\u00f3metros. El medio acuoso es el capacitor.\n",
    "- $W$, $L$: ancho y largo del canal (cm)\n",
    "- $V_{th}$: threshold voltage. En tu dispositivo tipo p es **negativo**\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 16,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "name": "stdout",
     "output_type": "stream",
     "text": [
      "Analizando muestra: 010626_batch4_mta1_03\n",
      "Usando V_DS = -0.400181 V\n",
      "curve=dict_keys(['v_gs', 'i_ds', 'v_ds', 'curve_name'])\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "# Realizar extracci\u00f3n de saturaci\u00f3n para una sola muestra\n",
    "print(\"Analizando muestra: \" + measurement_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "curves = read_all_curves(hdf5_path, measurement_name)\n",
    "\n",
    "i_max = max(range(len(curves)), key=lambda i: abs(curves[i]['v_ds'][0])) # Es el primer valor porque se repite para todas las mediciones.\n",
    "curve = curves[i_max]\n",
    "v_gs, i_ds, v_ds = curve['v_gs'], curve['i_ds'], curve['v_ds']\n",
    "print(f\"Usando V_DS = {v_ds[0]} V\\ncurve={curve.keys()}\") # Es el transfer m\u00e1s alto que asegura el r\u00e9gimen saturado para obtener el V_th\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 17,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "application/vnd.jupyter.widget-view+json": {
